## 1. Dark‑mode toggle (R1)

```tsx
// src/Settings.jsx
import { useContext } from 'react';
import { ThemeContext } from '../theme/ThemeProvider';

export default function Settings() {
  const { theme, toggleTheme } = useContext(ThemeContext);

  return (
    <section className="settings-page">
      {/* other setting fields */}
      <div className="toggle-container">
        <label htmlFor="dark-mode-toggle" className="toggle-label">
          Dark mode
        </label>
        <input
          id="dark-mode-toggle"
          type="checkbox"
          checked={theme === 'dark'}
          onChange={toggleTheme}
          className="toggle-input"
        />
      </div>

      {/* Save button – mobile fix below */}
      <button className="save-btn">Save</button>
    </section>
  );
}
```

`ThemeProvider` already provides `theme` (`'light' | 'dark'`) and `toggleTheme`. No header changes.

